---
import "../../styles/global.css";
---

<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <meta charset="utf-8" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1" />
    <meta
      name="description"
      content="A wall-mounted hexagon lighting piece built with a XIAO ESP32-C3, WS2812B LEDs, and capacitive touch controls."
    />
    <link rel="preconnect" href="https://rsms.me/" />
    <link rel="stylesheet" href="https://rsms.me/inter/inter.css" />
    <link rel="icon" type="image/svg+xml" href="/favicon.svg" />
    <title>Hexagon Lighting</title>
  </head>

  <body
    class="bg-[#0b1126] text-slate-200 selection:bg-[#aaccff] selection:text-[#113399]"
  >
    <div
      class="mx-auto min-h-screen max-w-screen-xl px-6 py-12 md:px-12 md:py-16 lg:py-0"
    >
      <div class="lg:flex lg:justify-between lg:gap-16">
        <header
          class="lg:sticky lg:top-0 lg:flex lg:h-screen lg:w-[38%] lg:min-w-[360px] lg:flex-col lg:justify-center lg:py-16 mb-10"
        >
          <div
            class="relative overflow-hidden rounded-3xl border border-white/10 bg-white/[0.035] p-8 shadow-2xl shadow-blue-950/20 backdrop-blur"
          >
            <div
              class="absolute -right-20 -top-20 h-56 w-56 rounded-full bg-blue-500/10 blur-3xl"
            >
            </div>

            <p
              class="mb-6 text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-[0.25em] text-[#aaccff]"
            >
              Project Writeup
            </p>

            <h1
              class="mb-4 text-4xl font-medium tracking-tight text-white sm:text-5xl lg:text-6xl"
            >
              Hexagon<br />Lighting
            </h1>

            <p class="max-w-sm text-base leading-7 text-slate-400">
              A wall-mounted desk lighting solution that doubles as a piece of
              modern art.
            </p>


            <nav class="mt-8 hidden lg:block">
              <div class="space-y-5">
                <a
                  href="#overview"
                  class="group flex items-center gap-5 text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-[0.2em] text-slate-500 transition hover:text-slate-200"
                >
                  <span
                    class="h-px w-10 bg-slate-600 transition-all group-hover:w-16 group-hover:bg-slate-300"
                  ></span>
                  Overview
                </a>

                <a
                  href="#construction"
                  class="group flex items-center gap-5 text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-[0.2em] text-slate-500 transition hover:text-slate-200"
                >
                  <span
                    class="h-px w-10 bg-slate-600 transition-all group-hover:w-16 group-hover:bg-slate-300"
                  ></span>
                  Build
                </a>

                <a
                  href="/projects"
                  class="group flex items-center gap-5 text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-[0.2em] text-[#aaccff] transition hover:text-white"
                >
                  <span
                    class="h-px w-10 bg-[#aaccff] transition-all group-hover:w-16"
                  ></span>
                  Return to Projects
                </a>
              </div>
            </nav>
          </div>
        </header>

        <main class="w-full lg:w-[62%] lg:py-24">
          <section id="overview" class="scroll-mt-16">
            <div
              class="overflow-hidden rounded-3xl border border-white/10 bg-white/[0.035]"
            >
              <img
                src="/images/hexagon-room.png"
                alt="Illuminated hexagon wall art"
                class="aspect-[16/9] w-full object-cover"
              />
            </div>
            <div class="mt-8">
              <p class="text-lg leading-8 text-slate-300">
                My sister's room had a simple lighting problem: the main fixture
                was centered in the room, so she cast a shadow over her desk. I
                made this wall-mounted decoration to improve the desk lighting
                while also making the wall more interesting.
              </p>
            </div>
          </section>

          <section id="construction" class="mt-20 scroll-mt-16">
            <div
              class="mt-0 grid gap-8 md:grid-cols-[1fr_1.1fr] md:items-center"
            >
              <div>
                <h2
                  class="text-xl font-semibold uppercase tracking-[0.22em] text-[#aaccff]"
                >
                  Construction
                </h2>
                <p class="mt-5 leading-7 text-slate-400">
                  The design was inspired by the Hexaleaf project on
                  Thingiverse. I liked the larger-hexagon arrangement, but the
                  original piece was too large, so I designed my own hexagons to
                  fit the space.
                </p>
                <p class="mt-4 leading-7 text-slate-400">
                  A XIAO ESP32-C3 handles the control logic and can connect to
                  home Wi-Fi for time data. TTP223 capacitive touch pads on the
                  lower hexagon provide user input for brightness and color.
                </p>
              </div>
              <div class="space-y-4">
                <img
                  src="/images/hexagon-inside.png"
                  alt="Inside of the bottom hexagon showing electronics"
                  class="w-full rounded-2xl border border-white/10"
                />
              </div>
            </div>
          </section>

          <section id="layout" class="mt-20 scroll-mt-16">
            <div
              class="mt-8 grid gap-8 md:grid-cols-[1.1fr_0.9fr] md:items-center"
            >
              <img
                src="/images/hexagon-layout.png"
                alt="LED path layout for the hexagon art"
                class="w-full rounded-2xl border border-white/10"
              />
              <div>
                <h2
                  class="mb-5 text-xl font-semibold uppercase tracking-[0.22em] text-[#aaccff]"
                >
                  Layout
                </h2>
                <p class="leading-7 text-slate-400">
                  The WS2812B LEDs allow each of the 14 smaller hexagons to have
                  its own color. Rather than making the LED path snake back and
                  forth unnecessarily, I used two parallel paths to simplify
                  assembly.
                </p>
                <p class="mt-4 leading-7 text-slate-400">
                  Each hexagon contains eight LEDs, which provides sufficient
                  even lighting. The bottom hexagon houses the controls, inputs,
                  and power jack.
                </p>
              </div>
            </div>

            <div class="mt-8 grid gap-4 sm:grid-cols-3">
              <img
                src="/images/hexagon-mounted.png"
                alt="Hexagon art raised from the wall"
                class="aspect-square w-full rounded-2xl border border-white/10 object-cover"
              />
              <img
                src="/images/hexagon-blue.png"
                alt="Blue hexagon lighting pattern"
                class="aspect-square w-full rounded-2xl border border-white/10 object-cover"
              />
              <img
                src="/images/hexagon-peach.png"
                alt="Peach hexagon lighting pattern"
                class="aspect-square w-full rounded-2xl border border-white/10 object-cover"
              />
            </div>
          </section>

          <section id="code" class="mt-20 scroll-mt-16">
            <h2
              class="text-xl font-semibold uppercase tracking-[0.22em] text-[#aaccff]"
            >
              Code
            </h2>
            <div class="mt-3">
              <p class="max-w-2xl leading-7 text-slate-400">
                I started with FastLED's Pacifica example and reverse engineered
                the mechanism behind its flowing color effect. I then created a
                seven-color palette: aquamarine, amethyst purple, lava orange,
                pine green, sapphire indigo, sunrise peach, and sunset gold.
              </p>
              <p class="mt-4 max-w-2xl leading-7 text-slate-400">
                The bottom-left capacitive touch pad cycles through the palette.
                Automatic brightness and a weather pattern were also considered,
                but the ESP32-C3 caused significant WS2812B flicker while
                connected to Wi-Fi. The device therefore grabs the time over NTP
                and turns Wi-Fi back off.
              </p>
            </div>

            <div class="mt-8 grid gap-4 sm:grid-cols-3">
              <img
                src="/images/hexagon-green.png"
                alt="Green hexagon palette pattern"
                class="aspect-square w-full rounded-2xl border border-white/10 object-cover"
              />
              <img
                src="/images/hexagon-indigo.png"
                alt="Indigo hexagon palette pattern"
                class="aspect-square w-full rounded-2xl border border-white/10 object-cover"
              />
              <img
                src="/images/hexagon-purple.png"
                alt="Purple hexagon palette pattern"
                class="aspect-square w-full rounded-2xl border border-white/10 object-cover"
              />
            </div>

            <div class="mt-8 grid gap-4 md:grid-cols-3">
              <article
                class="rounded-2xl border border-white/10 bg-white/[0.035] p-6"
              >
                <div class="text-sm text-[#aaccff]">01</div>
                <h3 class="mt-8 text-xl font-medium text-white">Night</h3>
                <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-6 text-slate-400">
                  LEDs off from 8:30 PM to 7:00 AM.
                </p>
              </article>
              <article
                class="rounded-2xl border border-white/10 bg-white/[0.035] p-6"
              >
                <div class="text-sm text-[#aaccff]">02</div>
                <h3 class="mt-8 text-xl font-medium text-white">Day</h3>
                <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-6 text-slate-400">
                  Full brightness from 7:00 AM to 8:20 PM.
                </p>
              </article>
              <article
                class="rounded-2xl border border-white/10 bg-white/[0.035] p-6"
              >
                <div class="text-sm text-[#aaccff]">03</div>
                <h3 class="mt-8 text-xl font-medium text-white">Fade</h3>
                <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-6 text-slate-400">
                  Brightness linearly decays from 8:20 to 8:30 PM.
                </p>
              </article>
            </div>

            <a
              href="https://github.com/Padimo/sunriseclock"
              target="_blank"
              rel="noreferrer"
              class="group mt-8 block self-start rounded-2xl border border-white/10 bg-white/[0.035] p-6 transition hover:border-[#aaccff]/40 hover:bg-white/[0.055]"
            >
              <span class="text-xs uppercase tracking-[0.2em] text-slate-500"
                >Source code</span
              >
              <div class="mt-5 text-xl font-medium text-white">
                github.com/Padimo/sunriseclock
              </div>
              <div
                class="mt-2 text-sm text-slate-500 transition group-hover:text-[#aaccff]"
              >
                View the project →
              </div>
            </a>
          </section>

          <section id="lessons" class="mt-20 scroll-mt-16 pb-24">
            <h2
              class="text-xl font-semibold uppercase tracking-[0.22em] text-[#aaccff]"
            >
              Final Thoughts
            </h2>
            <div class="mt-5">
              <p class="text-lg leading-8 text-slate-300">
                It took several iterations to get the hexagon size, LED path,
                and data connectivity working correctly. The finished piece was
                appreciated for its movement and color, but it still had
                usability problems.
              </p>
              <p class="mt-5 leading-7 text-slate-400">
                The power adapter's bright blue indicator had to be unplugged at
                night, which meant dealing with the boot flicker each morning.
                The evening auto-brightness transition was also too quick. The
                piece is beautiful, but it needs more work to become a practical
                everyday light.
              </p>
            </div>
            <div
              class="mt-10 flex items-center justify-between border-t border-white/10 pt-6 text-xs text-slate-600"
            >
              <span>Hexagon Lighting</span>
              <a href="#overview" class="transition hover:text-slate-300"
                >Back to top ↑</a
              >
            </div>
          </section>
        </main>
      </div>
    </div>
  </body>
</html>
